# DOM access and lifecycle

## Prefer `lwc:ref` over `querySelector`

- For stable template nodes (modals, panels, focus targets), prefer `lwc:ref` (API v59+) over `this.template.querySelector(...)`.
- `querySelector` breaks silently when class names or structure drift; refs are compiler-validated.

## Timer cleanup

- Clear **every** `setTimeout` / `setInterval` ID in `disconnectedCallback` when the callback touches component state.
- Do not assume only one timer exists (e.g. `_autoSaveTimer` and `_notifyTimer` both need cleanup).

## `renderedCallback` guards

- Avoid expensive work on every re-render (e.g. page-index lookup on each keystroke).
- Early-return when inputs relevant to the block (`pageId`, `activeIndex`, wired data identity) have not changed.
